I agree that messages arriving out of sequence would be a bug. 

But I don't think that this is a case of messages arriving
out of sequence.  

I think this is messages arriving in sequence about two 
different poisoned darts.

Consider the sequence: 

> Your dart is no longer poisoned.  The dart hits the dwarf.  The poison
> was deadly...

The "no longer poisoned" message happens when the poison wears off of 
your dart.  This can only happen after the dart hits. 

The "dart hits the dwarf" message happens whenever anybody's dart 
hits any dwarf.  Not necessarily the same dart.  Not necessarily 
even the same dwarf.  I think it's likely that a monster threw a 
dart at the OP and a dwarf - probably but not necessarily the one 
that the OP had just attacked - was in the way.

"The poison was deadly" indicates that something previously poisoned
was killed by poison.  That could be the dwarf hit by the first dart, 
who got poisoned as the poison wore off the dart.  It could be the 
dwarf that got hit by the second dart, if the second dart was also 
poisoned.  It could be an orc that got a poisoned dagger in the gut 
two rounds previously. 

Kudos to Nybes for pointing out the "second dart" possibility.

